  "notes": "Web 384 — ROUTE-SHEET-UPLOAD-FAILS-ON-PHONE-NOV8: the route-sheet file upload that refused Nirojini's sheet on her phone tonight (\"That file could not be read as a route sheet — nothing was saved\") is fixed. (1) The PDF reader (PDF.js 3.11.174) now ships WITH the app — js/vendor/pdf.min.js + js/vendor/pdf.worker.min.js, same-origin, tried FIRST; the CDN copy remains only as a backstop, and a failed reader load is no longer cached, so the next upload tries fresh instead of replaying a dead reader for the life of the page. A phone's dead network moment or a blocked CDN can no longer kill the read outright. (2) A file is routed by what it IS, not by what the picker called it: RouteSheetFile.sniffKind reads the first bytes (%PDF / JPEG / PNG / GIF / WebP magic) and only an unrecognised file falls back to the picker's labels — a PDF forwarded through a message app or drive picker with an empty type and a bare-number name now reaches the PDF reader instead of dying in the photo reader. (3) A PDF text read that fails no longer dead-ends at the refusal: the pages are tried through the photo (OCR) reader before anything is refused. A genuinely unreadable file still refuses plainly, and a failed read still never touches a saved route. modules/dispatch.js + the two new vendor files only; version stays 63.",
